--BIND
-- GENERATED by tools/classless-web/bindgen.py -- regenerate, do not hand-edit.
--
-- CLDB.bind[spellLineId] = { talentLineId, ... }
--
-- The talents each spell can be traded against. This is what the practice
-- mechanic offers instead of the spell's next rank -- put the work into
-- Fireball, or into what makes Fireball better.
--
-- Two ways in, and the order matters. The first entries for a spell are the
-- talents that genuinely MODIFY it, by the core's own test (same SpellClassSet,
-- overlapping EffectSpellClassMask -- SpellInfo::IsAffectingSpell). After them
-- come the talents that share its TREE but modify no single spell: the flat
-- stat, aura and proc ones. Those used to be bought from a separate tree pot,
-- which the measurement showed to be a dead end -- two purchases in 143,749
-- credited kills. An offer is capped at five, so the real modifiers are the
-- ones that fit.
--
-- 556 of 556 spell lines offer something. 418 talents by mask, 204 by tree,
-- 622 of 622 reachable in total.
if CLDB==nil then CLDB={} end
